# ==============================================================================
# Portfolio-Supplier-Spend-Consolidation-Dashboard — .gitattributes
#
# Added 2026-09-09 after the step-0 commit, which produced CRLF warnings on
# every text file. The warnings are harmless for .md, .sql and .py — Git's
# autocrlf handles them and the content is unaffected.
#
# THEY ARE NOT HARMLESS FOR step0-scaffold.sh.
#
# That file is now committed in a PUBLIC repository. If a Linux or macOS user
# clones it after a CRLF checkout, the shebang line reads `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`
# and the shell reports:
#
#     /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# — an error that gives no hint of its own cause. The rule below prevents it.
# ==============================================================================

# Default: let Git normalise line endings in the repository, check out native.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts MUST stay LF, in the repo and on disk, on every platform.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Keep these LF too — they are read by tools, not only by editors.
*.py text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf

# Documentation and data: normalise, check out native. Windows editors are the
# main consumer here.
*.md text
*.csv text
*.txt text

# Binary — never touch.
*.twbx binary
*.hyper binary
*.tde binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
